Summary
This article explains how to verify that your environment has successfully converted from EWS to Microsoft Graph in Compulaw Vision Sync for Exchange 4.00 or higher.
Discussion
Verify Configuration Setting
Confirm that the system is configured to use Microsoft Graph instead of EWS.
Open the synching.exe.config file.
Locate <UseEWSNoAnchorMbx>false</UseEWSNoAnchorMbx>.
Verify the value is set to <UseEWSNoAnchorMbx>false</UseEWSNoAnchorMbx>.
ValueResult
false
Syncs in Microsoft Graph API
true
Syncs in EWS API
Review Replacer Log for Successful Migration
Review the Replacer log to confirm that the migration completed successfully.
Default Log Location: C:\Program Files (x86)\Vision Sync for Exchange\Logs\
File Format: Replacer_<date>_<numbers>.log
Example: Replacer_20260512_101257.log
Open the most recent Replacer log file.
Scroll to the end of the log.
Verify === Migration completed successfully === displays.
Review the Processing Summary and Migration Results sections.
Locate the EWS Conversion Pending section.
Key indicators of success include:
Failed: 0
Skipped: 0
Successful equals Total Processed
In the EWS Conversion Pending section, focus on the future events value. If the log shows 0 future events are still EWS items, the conversion is successful.
Review Sync Log for Graph Usage
Review the sync log to confirm that synchronization is running through Microsoft Graph.
Default Log Location: C:\Program Files (x86)\Vision Sync for Exchange\Logs\
File Format: sync_<date>_<run>.log
Example: sync_20260511_5.log
Open the most recent sync log file.
Review the beginning of the run.
Confirm the log shows VisionSynch, Version=4.00.x.
Confirm the log shows Using MSGraph for Active Directory services..
Scroll to the end of the run.
Review the synchronization summary for errors and warnings.
At the end of a successful synchronization run, no errors or warnings display. If there are no errors or warnings, and the beginning of the log confirms MSGraph, the environment has been converted and is syncing through Microsoft Graph.
 
Note: If <UseEWSNoAnchorMbx>false</UseEWSNoAnchorMbx> is set and the sync log shows VisionSynch, Version=4.00.x, historical EWS items may still exist in Outlook calendars. These historical EWS items cannot be updated during Microsoft Graph runs of Vision Sync.
Optional: Convert Additional Historical EWS Items
If you need to convert older EWS items, update the Replacer configuration and run the process again.
Open the replacer.exe.config file.
Locate the start date setting.
Change the value from today-30 to include additional past dates.
Run the Replacer process again.
This converts older EWS items to Microsoft Graph so they can be updated, cleared, or otherwise managed.
